<title>USA: Deutsche Bank unit sets $550 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank unit sets $550 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from Deutsche Bank unit Deutsche Bank Financial was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p>The deal was increased from an initial size of $500 million to meet demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>BORROWER DEUTSCHE BANK FINANCIAL</p>
<p>AMT $550 MLN	 COUPON  07.50     MATURITY 04/25/09</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.594  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA2   YIELD   07.552    PAY FREQ SEMI</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P  AA-PLUS  SPREAD 70 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>*THE NOTES ARE GUARANTEED BY THE NY BRANCH)</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1675))</p>
</text>
